## Pack data

The data under `packs/*/` (currently the Mandarin pack in `packs/zh/`,
ported from the `hsk` project) is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

This reflects upstream share-alike terms: glosses and inflection data
originate from Wiktionary via kaikki.org (CC BY-SA 3.0), and frequency
data originates from hermitdave/FrequencyWords (CC BY-SA 4.0), both of
which require share-alike redistribution of derived data. Where a pack
directory has its own `attribution.json`, per-source and per-contributor
attribution is recorded there.

Build-time tools and models used to construct pack data (for example
part-of-speech taggers) may carry non-commercial or copyleft licences of
their own. These are used only while building a pack and ship nothing
into the built output, so they do not affect the licence of the shipped
engine or pack data.
